! C2H7O3Cl | caa005bTSb-hess: HESSIAN-ONLY precursor at wB97X-D/6-31G(d,p)/PCM(water)
!
! Step 1 of 2 for the TS refinement (caa005bTSb). Attempts to run
! RUNTYP=SADPOINT directly failed repeatedly: GAMESS's default HESS
! source for SADPOINT is READ (requiring an explicit $HESS group we don't
! have), and an explicit HESS=GUESS override, despite being confirmed
! valid syntax in docs-input.txt, did not take effect for reasons not
! fully understood (possibly a parser quirk specific to this keyword at a
! line-continuation boundary). Rather than keep guessing at $STATPT
! syntax, this switches strategy entirely: compute a genuine Hessian
! FIRST via a standalone RUNTYP=HESSIAN calculation (this file), then feed
! the result into the actual saddle-point search as a real $HESS block
! (matching exactly what the original, successful caa005bTSa.log did).
!
! RUNTYP=HESSIAN does not use $STATPT or $ZMAT at all (those groups are
! documented as only applying to RUNTYP=OPTIMIZE/SADPOINT) -- both removed
! here. $FORCE alone controls the Hessian computation (METHOD=SEMINUM,
! since wB97X-D has no analytic Hessian) and automatically punches the
! result to the .dat file in $HESS format at the end.
!
! Starting geometry: the same converged saddle point from caa005bTSa.log
! used in caa005bTSb.inp. Settings otherwise identical: wB97X-D,
! PCM(water), native GBASIS=N31 NGAUSS=6 NDFUNC=1 NPFUNC=1 (6-31G(d,p)).
!
! Next step once this completes: extract the punched $HESS block from
! caa005bTSb-hess.dat and insert it into a corrected caa005bTSb.inp with
! $STATPT HESS=READ (GAMESS's own default for SADPOINT), then run the
! actual saddle-point search.

 $CONTRL SCFTYP=RHF RUNTYP=HESSIAN DFTTYP=wB97X-D
         COORD=UNIQUE MAXIT=200 NOSYM=1
 $END
 $GUESS GUESS=HUCKEL $END
 $BASIS GBASIS=N31 NGAUSS=6 NDFUNC=1 NPFUNC=1 $END
 $SCF CONV=1.0D-6
     SOSCF=.T.
     DAMP=.F.
     SHIFT=.T.
     DIRSCF=.TRUE.
 $END
 $FORCE METHOD=SEMINUM PROJCT=.t. $END
 $PCM SOLVNT=WATER $END
 $SYSTEM MWORDS=100 MEMDDI=200 $END

 $DATA
